                      "text":  "Graph ML Learn Start here if you only know basic ML (vectors, matrices, neural nets). Part 1  -  Foundations Part 2  -  Core GNN Theory Part 3  -  Advanced Architectures Part 4  -  Practice \u0026amp; Frontier Quick Reference Part 1 - Foundations Start here if you only know basic ML (vectors, matrices, neural nets). Graph Foundations What is a graph, adjacency matrix, Laplacian, graph tasks, why graphs beat flat ML on relational data. Representation and Data Preparation Node/edge/graph features, building graphs from raw data, splits, leakage, PyTorch Geometric, DGL. Part 2 - Core GNN Theory The heart of graph deep learning: message passing and classic architectures. Message Passing Framework MPNN, permutation invariance/equivariance, aggregation, update - the unified view behind all GNNs. Classic Architectures GCN, GraphSAGE, GAT, GIN, MPNN - full math, intuition, code, and when to pick each. Spectral Methods Graph Fourier transform, ChebNet, spectral vs spatial convolution - where GCN really comes from. Part 3 - Advanced Architectures Going deeper: limitations, heterogeneous graphs, time, and transformers on graphs. Deep GNNs and Limitations Oversmoothing, over-squashing, expressiveness, Jumping Knowledge, residual connections, normalization. Heterogeneous and Knowledge Graphs R-GCN, HGT, metapaths, link prediction, knowledge graph embedding + GNN hybrids. Temporal and Dynamic Graphs Discrete snapshots, continuous-time (TGN), evolving graphs, temporal link prediction. Graph Transformers Graphormer, GPS, structure-aware attention, positional encodings on graphs. Part 4 - Practice and Frontier Training at scale, choosing GNNs, LLM integration, and latest research. Training, Optimization and Scaling Losses, sampling, mini-batch, full-graph, distributed training, frameworks, debugging. When to Use GNNs and Evaluation Decision framework, metrics, benchmarks, GNN vs MLP vs Transformer - honest tradeoffs. GNNs in the LLM Era Text-attributed graphs, GraphRAG, hybrid LLM+GNN systems, when graphs still matter. Recent Advances and Papers 2020–2026 breakthroughs, foundation models on graphs, surveys, thesis pointers, code repos. Quick Reference Formula cheat sheet: GNN Formula Sheet Key papers: Papers Hub"
